# Gripper + RTC (locked)

## Causal gripper (do not regress)

- **Ingest**: blend arms only; store **continuous** gripper raw. Never run GripperPost on `[k_now:]` (lookahead closes early on H=20).
- **Sample**: advance sticky binary SM only when the **active keyframe index** moves; hold last discrete between keys. Current + history only.
- Defaults: `close_enter=70`, `open_enter=40`, `close_confirm=2`, `open_confirm=5`, `min_close_hold_s=1.2`, `min_open_hold_s=0.35`, `blend_grippers=False`.

## Proven Costa handover launch (Orin → 192.168.0.100)

Prefer RTC + moderate send rate; H=20 early-grasp was fixed by causal SM, not by dropping H.

```bash
./scripts/start_async.sh \
  --host 192.168.0.100 --port 8003 \
  --protocol pi05 \
  --send-hz 10 --chunk-hz 30 --ctrl-hz 250 \
  --blend-s 0.12 --freeze-chassis \
  --gripper-binary \
  --gripper-close-enter 70 --gripper-open-enter 40 \
  --gripper-close-confirm 2 --gripper-open-confirm 5 \
  --gripper-min-close-hold-s 1.2 --gripper-min-open-hold-s 0.35
```

- Do **not** reintroduce ingest-time full-suffix gripper discretization.
- H=10 is safer if causal SM is absent; with causal SM, H=20 is OK.
- Uneven arm speed on traces is usually **policy rhythm** (only ~3/20 frames played), not RTT jitter.
